WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.400
Discover, price and protect: turning dashboards into paid work.

2
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:11.920
This is the video for module three of Power BI and Tableau: consulting, pricing and your dashboard career.

3
00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:18.460
Technical skill gets a dashboard built. Consulting skill gets it used and paid for.

4
00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:22.720
Most dashboard projects that fail do so before any chart is built.

5
00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:35.020
The analyst built what she assumed was needed, the data could not be accessed, or the dashboard could not be shared with the right people. A good discovery meeting prevents all three.

6
00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:44.630
Dashboard projects are also easy to underprice, because the charts take the least time, and clients cannot see the cleaning and checking.

7
00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:53.200
And to win work, you need proof. A small portfolio of well-explained projects beats a long list of tutorials.

8
00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:58.800
Plan 45 to 60 minutes, take notes, and cover five areas.

9
00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:05.720
Decisions. What will this dashboard help you decide? A dashboard that changes no decision will be abandoned.

10
00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:13.410
Audience. Who will view it, how often, and on what device? That decides the design and the phone layout.

11
00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:21.660
Data sources. Where does each number live today, and who can export it? Ask for a sample export before you quote.

12
00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:26.980
Refresh. How fresh must the data be, and who will press refresh?

13
00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:33.740
Access and privacy. Who may see what, and does the data include personal details?

14
00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:38.060
Afterwards, send a written summary and ask the client to correct it.

15
00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:49.330
Publish to web in Power BI, and Tableau Public, make your work visible to anyone. Use them for public data only, never for client or staff data.

16
00:01:50.580 --> 00:02:03.320
Row-level security lets one dashboard show each viewer only their own rows, such as a coordinator seeing only her state. It works only when shared through the service, not on a file you email.

17
00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:19.540
The Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 sets duties for anyone handling personal data. Collect only what you need, mask names and phone numbers, protect your devices, and delete copies when the project ends.

18
00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:24.160
Never send logins or data exports over open WhatsApp groups.

19
00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:35.910
For example, Chioma is quoting a two-page sales dashboard. She breaks it into phases. Discovery takes 4 hours. Data access and cleaning takes 16.

20
00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:42.810
The model and measures take 10 hours, and building two pages with a phone layout takes 12.

21
00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:50.030
Quality checks take 6 hours, and training and handover 4. That is 52 hours in total.

22
00:02:50.380 --> 00:03:00.180
Notice that cleaning is about 31% of the effort. Explain that to the client, and keep a record of actual hours so your next estimate improves.

23
00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:08.470
Now she prices it. Her rate of 15,000 naira per hour is for illustration only, not a market rate.

24
00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:23.770
52 hours gives a base price of 780,000 naira. She adds 15% contingency for unknown data problems, 117,000 naira, making 897,000.

25
00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:29.180
She rounds to a fixed 900,000 naira for the defined scope.

26
00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:40.880
Her payment plan is 450,000 naira deposit before starting, 270,000 when the first draft is approved, and 180,000 on handover.

27
00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:49.730
Protect your money. Take a deposit before starting, and receive payment through a traceable channel such as a bank transfer.

28
00:03:50.080 --> 00:04:00.450
Be wary of overseas clients who send too much and ask for a refund of the difference. That is a common scam. Never share banking passwords or one-time codes.

29
00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:05.920
And when the client asks for more, check the written scope and send a priced change request.

30
00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:16.230
To remember. Cover all five discovery areas. Use public tools only for public data. Estimate by phase and add contingency.

31
00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:24.160
Build three portfolio projects, each with a short case study of your decisions and checks, and never use client data in them.

32
00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:35.630
Now practise. Run a discovery meeting with a real person, price and propose the project, and write a 13-week plan with a number you can tick off each week.

33
00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:37.920
Continue with the lessons below.
